# Local publishing — the values scripts/release-ios.sh needs to do what CI does.
# Copy to .env.release, which is gitignored:
#
#   cp .env.release.example .env.release
#
# None of the SECRET values below belong in git. The two file references should
# point OUTSIDE this repository — the signing folder in CLAUDE.md — or, better,
# come from 1Password (see the bottom of this file), so nothing sensitive is
# ever written to a file in the working tree.
#
# team id and bundle id are NOT secret (they are already in the committed
# workflow and ExportOptions.plist) and default correctly in the script, so you
# only need APPLE_TEAM_ID here to override the default.

# --- App Store Connect API key ---------------------------------------------

# The key id is the ten characters in the .p8 filename (AuthKey_XXXXXXXXXX.p8).
# The issuer id is a team-wide UUID: App Store Connect → Users and Access →
# Integrations, shown once at the top of the App Store Connect API section.
# The key must hold the Admin role — App Manager fails at export (see docs).
APPSTORE_KEY_ID=3Q9B2S77U8
APPSTORE_ISSUER_ID=

# The .p8 itself, either as a path on disk or (from 1Password) as inline PEM.
APPSTORE_PRIVATE_KEY_PATH=/Users/patrick/workspace/git/wvvy/icloud-signing-keys/AuthKey_3Q9B2S77U8.p8

# --- Distribution certificate ----------------------------------------------

# The .p12 that carries the Apple Distribution + Development identities (the same
# signing.p12 CI base64-encodes into IOS_DIST_CERT_P12_BASE64) and its password.
# Either a path on disk, or the base64 blob from 1Password.
IOS_DIST_CERT_P12_PATH=/Users/patrick/workspace/git/wvvy/icloud-signing-keys/signing.p12
IOS_DIST_CERT_PASSWORD=

# --- 1Password (recommended) -----------------------------------------------
#
# Any value above can be an `op://vault/item/field` reference instead of the
# secret itself. When .env.release contains one, release-ios.sh re-runs itself
# under `op run`, which resolves every reference, injects the results as
# environment variables and masks them in the output — so no secret is ever
# written to this file or left in scrollback.
#
# Run scripts/1password-load.sh once to create the "WVVY iOS" item this expects,
# then replace the block above with the references below (drop the _PATH keys):
#
#   APPSTORE_KEY_ID="op://Private/WVVY iOS/key id"
#   APPSTORE_ISSUER_ID="op://Private/WVVY iOS/issuer id"
#   APPSTORE_PRIVATE_KEY="op://Private/WVVY iOS/p8"
#   IOS_DIST_CERT_P12_BASE64="op://Private/WVVY iOS/p12 base64"
#   IOS_DIST_CERT_PASSWORD="op://Private/WVVY iOS/p12 password"
#
# Optional override (defaults to 9DTLYZS258, which is already public):
#   APPLE_TEAM_ID="op://Private/WVVY iOS/team id"
